Hi, just found yet another server with IRQ problems: Fujitsu Siemens TX-150.

IRQs do work, but if you have high throughput (say 4 4Mbit MPEG2 transport 
streams coming from a DVB-T card), I get very bad corruption.

Tests: 
disable ACPI. no effect
disable ACPI AND APIC. everything starts working perfectly.

So looks like there are multiple causes of these IRQ issues all coming 
together, which explains why it is so had to fix.

Will start looking into this stuff again tonight or tomorrow.



